  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex but consistent relationship between estrone and Dipeptidyl peptidase IX (DPPX), with estrone acting as a target for multiple compounds that ultimately interact with DPPX. The core mechanism appears to involve estrone being a target of compounds that are themselves targets of DPPX, forming a chain of interactions. This suggests that estrone may be indirectly modulated by DPPX through a series of intermediate molecules, such as Emopamil-binding protein-like and Eupenifeldin. The high scores in all three paths indicate a strong, albeit indirect, connection, likely due to the shared pathway of DPPX in the metabolic processes of the target organisms. The presence of multiple compounds that target DPPX, including those that are also targets of estrone, implies that DPPX may play a role in the regulation of estrone through a metabolic or enzymatic cascade. The integration of these paths highlights the importance of DPPX in the broader context of estrone metabolism, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
